		(at 254 125.73 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "682c0125-846d-4a7b-bf61-0f52e0c65407")
	)
	(text "The controller drives each rail eFuse EN/UVLO pin directly - no FET. High turns the rail on,\nlow turns it off. EN/UVLO trips at 1.2V, so a 3.3V push-pull output drives it both ways."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 297.18 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "72a2cc44-609e-4037-9c6d-ba765aa5350a")
	)
	(text "The controller pins float during reset, so the 100k on each EN/UVLO net sets the boot state:\npull-up to +3V3 = rail on, pull-down = rail off. Note this is the opposite direction from the\nold FET-gate version - the pull now sits on the eFuse pin, not on a gate.\n\n#176 should leave EN/UVLO as a plain logic input with no divider from the rail input; VSYS\nundervoltage is already enforced by the pack eFuse on #173. If a divider is kept there, the\n100k has to be folded into its math - it shifts the UVLO trip point."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 297.18 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "74d8320e-60e0-4741-b9b6-daa620bd4864")
	)
